<title>NETHERLANDS: Lanschot cuts Ceteco to underperformer.</title>
<headline>Lanschot cuts Ceteco to underperformer.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summary of Feb 26 research.</p>
<p>Company---------Sector--------Price---Broker----------------</p>
<p>Ceteco	    Trade	   104.50  Van Lanschot</p>
<p>COMMENT: UNDERPERFORMANCE (From hold). Ceteco's 1996-results were somewhat disappointing. Ceteco offers credit facilities on its goods in South America to increase its market share. Interest charges rose 75 pct to DFl 52.8 million in 1996 and charges are expected to increase. These credit facilities are crucial for success in the Latin American retail market but it also increases its business risk profile. Ceteco will not be able to realise +10 pct EPS growth in the coming years.</p>
<p>    Estimates (NLG):  EPS	  P/E    P/CF   Dividend</p>
<p>    1996 (actual)     3.72	 28.1   20.0    0.75</p>
<p>    1997		  4.05	 25.8   17.2    0.85</p>
<p>    1998		  4.45	 23.5   15.5    0.90</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000 (Fax +31 20 504 5040)</p>
